WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.380
I'm Jenna Fisher, and I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是珍娜·费舍，我是安吉拉·金赛。

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.220
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.360
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你们打造了终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

4
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.340
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office
每周，我们都将深入探索《办公室》的世界

5
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.060
with exclusive interviews, behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
带来独家访谈、幕后花絮以及许许多多的闺蜜故事。

6
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.080
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士 6.0版》。

7
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:25.730
Hi.
嗨。

8
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:26.810
Hello there.
你好呀。

9
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.070
What's up?
怎么啦？

10
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.030
What's up with you?
你最近怎么样？

11
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:29.890
I don't know.
我不知道。

12
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.350
You kind of got that look that, I don't know, is something going on?
你刚才那种表情，怎么说呢，是有什么事吗？

13
00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:34.290
You have that look.
你就是那种表情。

14
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.050
You're like, ew.
你好像在说，呃。

15
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:39.910
No, I'm just excited to be here because we're coming back from a little bit of a vacation.
不，我只是很高兴能来到这里，因为我们刚结束了一个小长假。

16
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:40.990
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

17
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:44.170
And so I'm just, like, excited to be sitting here face-to-face.
所以我只是觉得很兴奋，能坐在这里面对面聊天。

18
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.050
You're just happy, and I'm like, what's going on?
你挺高兴的，而我在想，发生什么事了？

19
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.190
No, I know.
不，我懂。

20
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.630
What have you been up to?
你最近都在忙什么？

21
00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.050
I haven't seen you in two weeks, lady.
我有两个星期没见你了，老搭档。

22
00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:51.950
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

23
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:58.230
Well, okay, our kids are doing these summer, like, college programs
好吧，是这样的，我们的孩子在参加那种暑期大学项目

24
00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.610
where you go to a university.
就是去一所大学里上学。

25
00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.830
They had to apply, and they go to a university.
他们必须申请，然后去大学里。

26
00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.190
Isabel and Jack are doing this.
伊莎贝尔和杰克就在参加这个。

27
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.470
They live in a dorm for four weeks.
他们在宿舍里住四个星期。

28
00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.790
They take a course.
他们要上一门课。

29
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.670
They get three college credits out of it.
他们能从中获得三个大学学分。

30
00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.650
You know, they're going to be seniors in high school next year.
你知道的，他们明年就要读高三了。

31
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:13.890
Yeah.
对啊。

32
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.750
But this is, like, a true, like, hey, here's what college is going to be like.
但这就像是一次真正的体验，嘿，大学生活会是什么样子的。

33
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:19.590
A little bit, right?
有点像，对吧？

34
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.750
It's a little practice run.
这是一次小型预演。

35
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.030
Because you, like, moved them into the dorm rooMs.
因为你得帮他们把行李搬进宿舍。

36
00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.130
Like, they're getting a whole dorm room thing.
就像，他们要经历整个宿舍的那一套流程。

37
00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:25.690
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

38
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:30.290
They each have roommates that they didn't know until they got there and signed in.
他们都有室友，而且是到了那里签到后才知道是谁。

39
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:31.850
They found out who their roommate was.
他们到了才知道自己的室友是谁。

40
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.890
You know, we had to do that thing where we got bins, and we labeled everything,
你知道的，我们得做那种准备工作，买收纳箱，给所有东西贴上标签

41
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.670
and we packed it all up.
然后把它们全都打包好。

42
00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:43.330
And we got there, and the two different dorms they're in, one of them,
等我们到了那里，他们住的两栋不同的宿舍楼里，其中一栋

43
00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.110
the line for the elevator to move in was so long because everyone showed up with their parents.
搬家时的电梯队伍长得不得了，因为大家都带着父母一起来了。

44
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.050
So Isabel's on the fourth floor.
所以伊莎贝尔住在四楼。

45
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.430
Josh is like, let's just take the stairs, lady.
乔希就说，咱们直接走楼梯吧，女士。

46
00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:53.850
What?
什么？

47
00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:54.450
Yes.
没错。

48
00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:59.710
We moved her in just walking upstairs all day carrying things.
我们一整天都在爬楼梯搬东西，把她送进了宿舍。

49
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.150
And Josh is very fit.
而且乔希身体非常健壮。

50
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.870
I am not as fit.
我可没那么健壮。

51
00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:10.610
You are fit, but there's a difference between, like, you have a type of, like, tennis fitness.
你身体很健康，但两者的区别在于，比如，你有一种，比如说，网球运动员的那种体能。

52
00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:11.270
Yes.
是的。

53
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.990
It doesn't translate to, like, power stepping and climbing.
这并不适用于，比如说，强力踏步和攀爬。

54
00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:16.530
Right.
对的。

55
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.630
Anyway, so I am sore today, but we got them moved in.
总之，我今天浑身酸痛，但我们总算把他们搬进去了。

56
00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:24.330
By the time you guys hear this, they will have completed their program.
等你们听到这期节目时，他们的项目就已经结束了。

57
00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.710
But that's what I've been up to.
不过这就是我最近在忙的事情。

58
00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.050
I've been packing up two teenagers and taking them off to this college
我一直在收拾两个青少年的行李，带他们去这所大学

59
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.770
and getting them moved into a dorm room, and now they're there.
把他们安顿进宿舍，现在他们已经在那里了。

60
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.710
And, like, we get calls, like, Isabel's like, I'm going to do laundry,
而且，我们还会接到电话，比如伊莎贝尔说，我要去洗衣服了，

61
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.170
but they don't take coins anymore.
但他们现在不收硬币了。

62
00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:39.850
I'm like, what?
我说，什么？

63
00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:40.770
How do you do laundry?
那你怎么洗衣服？

64
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.370
I would save up my coins.
我以前都会攒下硬币。

65
00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:47.130
Of course, a Ziploc bag full of coins for the parking meters and the laundry.
当然，一整袋塑料袋装的硬币，用来付停车费和洗衣费。

66
00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.490
I didn't even think about it.
我甚至都没想过这回事。

67
00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.970
It's all an app now.
现在全都是用手机应用了。

68
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.590
There's, like, the laundry app.
甚至还有什么洗衣应用。

69
00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.270
Don't get me started.
别让我开启这个话题。

70
00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.230
Do you know how many apps they've had to download?
你知道他们必须下载多少个应用吗？

71
00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.190
There's so many apps.
应用实在是太多了。

72
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:58.550
We don't want to look at our phones that much,
我们本来不想花那么多时间看手机，

73
00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.250
but, like, you need an app for everything.
但是，什么东西都需要一个应用。

74
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.590
We got a garage door.
我们装了个车库门。

75
00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.510
And the garage door guy was like,
然后装车库门的人就问，

76
00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.890
do you want an app on your phone to open and close your garage door?
你想在手机上装个应用来开门和关车库门吗？

77
00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:08.690
I said, I don't.
我说，我不想。

78
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.550
You know what I want?
你知道我想要什么吗？

79
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.930
I want a freaking button that I hold in my hand.
我想要一个我能拿在手里的该死的按钮。

80
00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:12.110
Give me a clicker.
给我一个遥控器。

81
00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.430
Give me a clicker, please.
求求你，给我一个遥控器吧。

82
00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.190
He was like, settle down, lady.
他当时说，冷静点，女士。

83
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.590
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

84
00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.770
I triggered you asking you about an app.
我问你关于应用的事，把你惹毛了。

85
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:19.990
But I was like, well, you did.
但我当时就想，好吧，你确实把我惹毛了。

86
00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:20.830
I know.
我知道。

87
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:21.970
Everything's an app now.
现在什么都是应用。

88
00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:22.370
Yeah.
是啊。

89
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.890
Anyway, it's good to see you.
总之，很高兴见到你。

90
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:25.550
How have you been?
你最近怎么样？

91
00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.430
I've been good.
我挺好的。

92
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:29.190
You know, Lee's movie, Nimrods, comes out very soon.
你知道的，李的电影《呆头鹅》很快就要上映了。

93
00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:29.930
I know.
我知道。

94
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.990
And we are trying to figure out our red carpet looks.
我们正在琢磨走红毯的造型。

95
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.250
Because, lady, the whole family is walking the red carpet.
因为，女士，我们全家人都要走红毯。

96
00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.950
And we've never done this before.
而且我们以前从来没经历过这个。

97
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.670
So, number one, I'm just trying to wrap my head around that.
所以，首先，我正努力在脑海里接受这件事。

98
00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.930
Like, what is that?
话说，那到底是什么样的？

99
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.690
How do I prepare them for that experience?
我该如何帮他们为那种经历做好准备？

100
00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.470
What's the impact of that experience going to be?
那次经历会带来什么影响？

101
00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.770
But then also, what are we wearing?
不过话说回来，我们该穿什么呢？

102
00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.270
Like, are you going to coordinate?
比方说，你们打算穿得有默契一点吗？

103
00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.770
These are the questions we're asking.
这就是我们正在探讨的问题。

104
00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:55.870
I don't think so.
我觉得不用吧。

105
00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.210
That feels too complicated.
那样感觉太复杂了。

106
00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.430
It feels like a...
感觉就像……

107
00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:58.850
And too precious.
而且太刻意了。

108
00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.450
It feels like a Christmas card.
感觉就像圣诞贺卡一样。

109
00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:00.910
Right.
对啊。

110
00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:01.250
Right?
是吧？

111
00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.430
You don't need to be a Christmas card tableau.
没必要弄得像圣诞贺卡合影一样。

112
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.410
And I love a coordinating Christmas card.
而且我很喜欢风格统一的圣诞贺卡。

113
00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.150
Don't get me wrong.
别误会我的意思。

114
00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:06.950
Oh, I know.
噢，我懂的。

115
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.930
But maybe for the red carpet, you all have your own looks.
不过也许在红毯上，你们每个人都穿自己的风格。

116
00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.430
Well, we all have our own ideas.
嗯，我们每个人都有自己的想法。

117
00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:16.930
I know Isabel did a red carpet once, and you gave me her dress that she wore.
我知道伊莎贝尔有一次走过红毯，你把她穿过的那件裙子送给了我。

118
00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:17.810
It's beautiful.
那条裙子很漂亮。

119
00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.990
And you were like, one day, if Harper ever needs it, and she was around this same age.
当时你说，总有一天，如果哈珀需要的话，而且她差不多也是这个年纪。

120
00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:26.070
Yes, my friend had produced the movie Mulan, the live action.
对，我朋友制作了真人版电影《花木兰》。

121
00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:26.510
Yeah.
对。

122
00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:27.690
And we went and saw it.
然后我们去看了。

123
00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.970
Me and Isabel and Jack.
我和伊莎贝尔还有杰克。

124
00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.390
And Jack wore a suit and Isabel wore a dress.
杰克穿了西装，伊莎贝尔穿了裙子。

125
00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.150
It was really cute.
真的超可爱。

126
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.010
We got it at the mall.
我们是在商场买的。

127
00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.130
It's really a cute dress.
那真的是一条很可爱的裙子。

128
00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.130
Oh, it's beautiful.
噢，太漂亮了。

129
00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:35.970
It's beautiful.
真的好漂亮。

130
00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.610
Well, unfortunately, the dress doesn't fit.
不过不巧的是，裙子穿不下了。

131
00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.870
I was worried about that because I gave it to you like two years ago, and I'm like,
我之前就担心这个，因为我大概两年前给你的，当时我想着……

132
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.110
I don't know if it's going to fit her.
我不知道她还能不能穿。

133
00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:44.650
Yeah.
是啊。

134
00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:47.390
I don't even know where to get clothes for myself for the red carpet.
我连自己走红毯的衣服该去哪里找都不知道。

135
00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:47.810
I know.
我懂的。

136
00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.310
I don't know what we're all going to wear.
我也不知道我们到时候都要穿什么。

137
00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.850
I hate red carpets.
我讨厌走红毯。

138
00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:51.430
I know.
我知道。

139
00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.390
I know.
我懂的。

140
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.650
I'm excited for the movie.
我很期待这部电影。

141
00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.270
I will be on the red carpet with you.
我会陪你一起走红毯的。

142
00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:56.910
Yes, you will.
对，你会的。

143
00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.250
I don't have an outfit.
我还没有行头呢。

144
00:04:58.470 --> 00:04:58.830
No.
没有。

145
00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.510
We should really be thinking about this because it's happening.
我们真的该好好想想这事了，因为马上就要来了。

146
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:01.930
I know.
我知道。

147
00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:02.510
It's exciting.
这让人很兴奋。

148
00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.130
The movie comes out August 14th, everybody, in theaters worldwide.
这部电影将于8月14日上映，各位，全球各大影院同步上映。

149
00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:06.830
Worldwide.
全球同步。

150
00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:07.610
Global.
全球公映。

151
00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:08.870
Global release.
全球上映。

152
00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:15.150
Oh, but also, lady, they are doing special early screenings of Nimrods in select theaters.
哦，对了，女士，他们还将在部分影院举办《笨蛋》的特别提前点映。

153
00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:18.730
It's happening on Tuesday, August 11th.
时间就在8月11日星期二。

154
00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:23.190
So, everyone, check the listings at your local theaters and see if they have one of the early
所以，大家快去查看当地影院的排片表，看看有没有

155
00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:23.850
screenings.
提前点映场。

156
00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:28.990
My folks, my sister, and some of my high school friends, they all got tickets to one of the
我爸妈、我妹妹还有一些高中朋友，他们都买到了

157
00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.230
early screenings in St. Louis.
圣路易斯提前点映场的票。

158
00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:30.770
Aww.
噢。

159
00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:31.470
I know.
我知道。

160
00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.210
I'm so excited for them to see it.
我太为他们高兴能看到这部电影了。

161
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.890
Well, it's such a fun movie to see with a group of people in the theater.
对啊，在影院里和大家一起看这部电影一定超有意思。

162
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.730
Yes, in the theater because, of course, there's all the great music in it, too.
没错，在影院看，因为当然了，里面还有超棒的音乐。

163
00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:40.970
Oh, yeah.
