这简直是板上钉钉，以至于那年他们让斯蒂芬·科尔伯特和乔恩·斯图尔特来颁这个奖，因为这本来会是一场《每日秀》同事在台上的重聚。

616
00:25:37.920 --> 00:25:40.220
And they were going to give it to their friend, Steve Carell.
他们本来要把奖颁给他们的朋友史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

617
00:25:40.800 --> 00:25:49.460
And then I believe Ricky Gervais ended up winning for the show Extras, which was a BBC show that HBO had just bought and like thrown on the air.
然后我记得瑞奇·热维斯最终凭《临时演员》获奖了，那是HBO刚买下并刚播出的一个BBC节目。

618
00:25:49.580 --> 00:25:50.560
And he wasn't even there.
他甚至都没到现场。

619
00:25:50.560 --> 00:25:53.880
It was one of those deals where they showed a black and white photo of him on the screen.
那是那种在屏幕上放一张他的黑白照片的场合之一。

620
00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:56.620
And they were like, Ricky Gervais isn't here.
他们说，瑞奇·热维斯没来。

621
00:25:56.740 --> 00:25:59.280
So instead, we're going to give this to our friend Steve Carell.
所以相反，我们要把这个颁给我们的朋友史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

622
00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:02.380
And then Steve jumped up and ran on stage and like bowed and everyone cheered.
然后史蒂夫一下子跳起来跑上台鞠躬，所有人都欢呼了。

623
00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:09.640
But I remember thinking of all of the robberies that occurred from folks who worked on The Office over the years,
但我记得回想这些年《办公室》演员们遭遇的所有痛失奖项，

624
00:26:09.800 --> 00:26:13.600
that season three best actor in a comedy was number one on my liSt.
第三季的喜剧类最佳男主角绝对排在我的榜单第一位。

625
00:26:13.600 --> 00:26:20.060
Because he was the funniest person in America and he was the best actor on a comedy in America by a wide margin.
因为他是美国最搞笑的人，而且以绝对优势成为了美国喜剧界演技最好的演员。

626
00:26:20.260 --> 00:26:24.820
And I always think of that performance in that episode as exhibit A in that argument.
我每次想到那一集里的表演，都觉得那是这个论点的头号证据。

627
00:26:25.140 --> 00:26:25.320
Yeah.
对。

628
00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:26.820
He's fantastic in it.
他在里面棒极了。

629
00:26:26.920 --> 00:26:27.040
Yeah.
对。

630
00:26:27.040 --> 00:26:29.300
And he never won an Emmy for the role of Michael Scott.
而且他从来没有因为迈克尔·斯科特这个角色赢得过艾美奖。

631
00:26:29.300 --> 00:26:29.660
He never did.
他从来没有。

632
00:26:29.660 --> 00:26:30.280
He never did.
他确实没有。

633
00:26:30.420 --> 00:26:37.940
When I speak to acting classes, I remind them of that fact that you can do the best work.
每当我给表演班做讲座时，我都会提醒他们这个事实：你可能做出最棒的作品。

634
00:26:37.940 --> 00:26:40.660
You can be the very, very best at what you do.
你可能在你的领域里做到绝对最优秀。

635
00:26:40.900 --> 00:26:41.100
Yeah.
对。

636
00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:41.640
I know.
我知道。

637
00:26:41.920 --> 00:26:48.980
At this point, it's like you can make a better cast and show out of the folks who have never won than the folks who have won, I dare say.
到了这个地步，我敢说，你可以用那些从未获奖的人组成一个比得过奖的人更棒的演员阵容和节目。

638
00:26:49.200 --> 00:26:50.840
And he's, you know, he's the lead.
而且你知道的，他可是男主角。

639
00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:51.400
Yeah.
对。

640
00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:53.340
They had a camera on us.
他们把摄像机对着我们。

641
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:54.680
I've told this story before.
我以前讲过这个故事。

642
00:26:55.240 --> 00:26:56.340
We were in a row together.
我们坐在一排。

643
00:26:56.560 --> 00:26:59.880
It was like Jenna and John and me in the same row.
就像詹娜、约翰和我就坐在同一排。

644
00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:01.500
And Steve was in front of us.
而史蒂夫坐在我们前面。

645
00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:06.280
And, you know, when they're announcing the nominees, the camera guys just run right up.
而且，你知道的，当他们宣布提名者时，摄影师直接就冲了过来。

646
00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:06.530
Right.
没错。

647
00:27:06.530 --> 00:27:07.540
And they just put a camera on.
然后他们就把镜头对准了。

648
00:27:07.660 --> 00:27:07.840
Right in your face.
直接怼到你脸上。

649
00:27:07.940 --> 00:27:08.620
Right in your face.
直接怼到你脸上。

650
00:27:08.720 --> 00:27:10.260
And so it's right in Steve's face.
所以它就直接怼在史蒂夫的脸上。

651
00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:12.140
And then we're directly behind him.
然后我们就紧跟在他身后。

652
00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:15.920
And when they didn't say his name, I guess I said, mother f***er.
当他们没有念到他的名字时，我想我说的是，操他妈的。

653
00:27:18.500 --> 00:27:20.220
I mean, that's the correct response.
我的意思是，这才是正常的反应。

654
00:27:20.580 --> 00:27:20.780
Yeah.
是啊。

655
00:27:21.180 --> 00:27:24.680
And I had one or two friends say, did you say mother f***er?
有一两个朋友问我，你是不是说操他妈的？

656
00:27:24.840 --> 00:27:26.400
I think I saw you say that.
我想我看到你这么说了。

657
00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:27.520
And I'm like, yes.
我说，是的。

658
00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:28.180
Yes, I did.
是的，我说了。

659
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:28.980
It came out of me.
那是情不自禁脱口而出的。

660
00:27:29.060 --> 00:27:30.080
I didn't have a choice.
我别无选择。

661
00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:32.060
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

662
00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:32.580
I couldn't.
我真的不敢相信。

663
00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:35.120
And I, you know, so many of us couldn't because he was amazing.
而且你知道，我们很多人都不敢相信，因为他太棒了。

664
00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:40.020
The other scene in that episode that I think of when I think of how great he was is the one where,
那集里让我印象深刻的另一个场景，每当我想起他有多棒时就会想起，那就是……

665
00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:44.800
so the plot is that he and Dwight decide that they're going to go to David Wallace's house.
剧情是这样的，他和德怀特决定去大卫·华莱士家。

666
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:45.120
Yes.
没错。

667
00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:48.920
And just like stop him and like make their argument why Scranton shouldn't close.
直接去堵他，当面陈述为什么斯克兰顿分公司不应该被关闭。

668
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:50.440
And he never shows up.
结果大卫根本没出现。

669
00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:52.820
They just end up spending the entire day outside his house.
他们最后在他家门外待了一整天。

670
00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:57.760
And he and Dwight are sitting there at the end when it looks like all is loSt.
最后当一切看起来都无望时，他和德怀特坐在那里。

671
00:27:57.760 --> 00:28:04.920
And he just says like, all right, top three, what are your top three moments ever, your three favorite moments at Dunder Mifflin?
他突然说，好吧，前三名，你一生中排名前三的时刻是什么？你在邓德米弗林最喜欢的三个时刻？

672
00:28:05.200 --> 00:28:12.880
And Dwight names a couple, one or two things I think we've seen in the world of the show, like the concussion, like when Michael took Dwight.
德怀特说出了几个，有一两个我觉得我们在剧里见过的，比如脑震荡那次，迈克尔带着德怀特。

673
00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:13.760
It took him to the hospital.
带他去了医院。

674
00:28:14.340 --> 00:28:15.420
And Dwight gets a little emotional.
德怀特有点动情了。

675
00:28:15.740 --> 00:28:15.980
Gets a little emotional.
有点动情了。

676
00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:21.840
And there's also one thing I think that we didn't see that was a reference to something that happened before the documentary started shooting.
还有一件事我觉得我们没见过，那是对纪录片开拍前发生的事情的一个梗。

677
00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:25.340
And then Dwight says, what about you?
然后德怀特问，那你呢？

678
00:28:25.440 --> 00:28:26.380
What are your top three moments?
你最棒的三大时刻是什么？

679
00:28:26.620 --> 00:28:31.360
And he says, all of them, every single moment, every single moment was wonderful and perfect and special.
他说，全部，每一个时刻，每一个时刻都那么美好、完美而特殊。

680
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:33.580
And it's really a beautiful moment.
这真的是一个非常动人的时刻。

681
00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:37.480
And then Dwight says, what about when Jan came and told you the office was closing?
然后德怀特说，那简来通知你办公室要关闭的时候呢？

682
00:28:37.580 --> 00:28:38.660
And he's like, God damn it, Dwight.
他当时就说，操蛋，德怀特。

683
00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:41.060
It was so perfect.
这太完美了。

684
00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:43.760
Dwight, like who he is.
德怀特就是这样的人。

685
00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:44.020
Yeah.
对。

686
00:28:44.220 --> 00:28:44.920
He's so literal.
他太较真了。

687
00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:47.580
He's extremely, every single moment.
他极其较真，每一个时刻。

688
00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:48.760
Well, I can think of one.
嗯，我能想到一个。

689
00:28:48.900 --> 00:28:49.100
Yeah.
对。

690
00:28:49.100 --> 00:28:58.880
He also, they did this great thing where Dwight is going to practice being David Wallace and Michael's going to plea his case, why they can't close Scranton Branch.
他们还有一个很棒的桥段，德怀特练习扮演大卫·华莱士，而迈克尔则要为斯克兰顿分公司为什么不能关闭进行陈述。

691
00:28:59.580 --> 00:29:04.800
And Dwight's just very matter of factly is like, well, it's a dying business for one.
德怀特非常公事公办地说，首先，这是一项垂死的业务。

692
00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:07.820
And it's like, it just comes down to numbers.
这说到底就是数字问题。

693
00:29:07.980 --> 00:29:08.760
It's just math.
这就是数学。

694
00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:10.780
And he's so matter of fact.
他表现得非常实事求是。

695
00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:12.380
And Michael's like, stop it, stop it.
迈克尔说，住手，住手。

696
00:29:12.460 --> 00:29:13.640
He's never going to say that.
他绝不会这么说。

697
00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:16.900
Well, there's a wonderful moment that was improvised between the two of them.
嗯，他们两个之间有一个非常精彩的即兴发挥时刻。

698
00:29:16.900 --> 00:29:21.440
I think the way it ended was Michael was like, just start over and be more scared of me.
我想最后迈克尔说的是，重新开始，而且要更怕我一点。

699
00:29:21.880 --> 00:29:26.200
And so Dwight goes back and he wasn't supposed to do this, but Rain walked up again.
于是德怀特回去重来，他本来不该这么做，但雷恩又走了过去。

700
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.520
And Michael's was like, David Wallace.
迈克尔当时说，大卫·华莱士。

701
00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:29.460
And Rain goes, ha!
然后雷恩说，哈！

702
00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:31.400
And jumps backwards.
然后往后一跳。

703
00:29:32.780 --> 00:29:34.200
And we had to cut it off.
然后我们不得不把它剪掉。

704
00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:38.980
Literally the frame where we cut it off is the last frame before they both started laughing.
字面意思上，我们剪掉的那一帧，就是他们两个开始笑之前的最后一帧。

705
00:29:39.300 --> 00:29:41.640
It's a good memory of that moment.
这是对那个时刻美好的回忆。

706
00:29:41.640 --> 00:29:43.940
Well, it was really fun to re-watch it.
嗯，重看这段真的很有趣。

707
00:29:44.140 --> 00:29:45.300
I highly recommend, guys.
我强烈推荐，伙计们。

708
00:29:45.600 --> 00:29:49.060
Well, since we're talking about season three, this is actually a question I wanted to ask you.
好吧，既然我们在聊第三季，这其实是我一直想问你们的一个问题。

709
00:29:49.480 --> 00:29:52.840
The arc of season three is such an impressive arc.
第三季的剧情弧光真是令人印象深刻。

710
00:29:53.060 --> 00:29:55.360
You have the whole storyline of Jim going to Stanford.
你们有吉姆去斯坦福的整条故事线。

711
00:29:55.380 --> 00:29:57.300
You had to create this whole other branch.
你们必须创造出另一个分公司。

712
00:29:57.440 --> 00:30:03.400
You had to fill it with people who were then going to come merge with the Scranton branch.
你们必须用那些随后要来和斯克兰顿分公司合并的人把这里填满。

713
00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:05.740
And then some of them stay.
然后他们中的一些人留了下来。

714
00:30:05.940 --> 00:30:07.520
Like you had to cast Rashida Jones.
比如你们必须挑选拉什达·琼斯。

715
00:30:07.680 --> 00:30:09.140
You had to cast Ed HelMs.
你们必须挑选艾德·赫尔姆斯。

716
00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:12.360
It was this massive ongoing storyline.
这是一个庞大的持续性故事线。

717
00:30:13.020 --> 00:30:15.660
Like, can you talk a little bit about how that was created?
比如，能稍微聊聊这是怎么创作出来的吗？

718
00:30:15.840 --> 00:30:20.940
Like some of the conversations in the room and like how far into the season did you get when we started shooting?
比如编剧室里的一些对话，还有在我们开始拍摄时，进度推进到这一季的什么阶段了？

719
00:30:21.180 --> 00:30:22.100
It's a great question.
这是个好问题。

720
00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:28.000
This was a big swing that Greg decided to make, which was at the end of season two after Jim and Pam kiss.
这是格雷格决定做出的一记大动作，那就是在第二季末尾吉姆和帕姆接吻之后。

721
00:30:28.520 --> 00:30:33.740
And Pam sort of lets him down in her mind easy, but for him not very easy.
帕姆在她自己看来算是比较轻松地拒绝了他，但对他来说可一点也不轻松。

722
00:30:34.340 --> 00:30:35.460
Greg was like, he's got to leave.
格雷格当时的想法是，他必须离开。

723
00:30:35.460 --> 00:30:39.740
We can't just start season three with him like back at the office.
我们不能直接让第三季从他回到办公室开始。

724
00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:43.140
It's not sort of following through on the story we've told.
那算不上对我们所讲述的故事的贯彻。

725
00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:45.820
The story we've told is that Jim stays in this office because of Pam.
我们所讲述的故事是，吉姆留在办公室是因为帕姆。

726
00:30:46.080 --> 00:30:49.500
And so if he makes a play for Pam and Pam turns him down, he's going to leave.
所以如果他向帕姆表白而帕姆拒绝了他，他是会离开的。

727
00:30:50.220 --> 00:30:52.820
So he had a general with Ed, I remember.
所以我记得他跟艾德有过一次会面。

728
00:30:53.140 --> 00:30:55.280
Like, and we were all Daily Show fans.
而且，我们当时都是《每日秀》的粉丝。

729
00:30:55.380 --> 00:30:56.760
And so we were like, oh, Ed Helms is here.
所以我们当时就想，哦，艾德·赫尔姆斯来了。

730
00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:57.180
That's fun.
这很有意思。

731
00:30:58.180 --> 00:31:02.460
And we came into that season and Greg was like, Jim is going to leave.
然后我们进入那一季的时候，格雷格就说，吉姆要走了。

732
00:31:02.660 --> 00:31:04.160
He's going to go to another branch.
他要去另一个分公司。

733
00:31:04.420 --> 00:31:07.720
We're going to meet an entire group of people who work in that branch.
我们会遇到一个在那个分公司工作的全新群体。

734
00:31:07.940 --> 00:31:11.100
And then at some point early in the season, they're going to fold together.
然后在那一季刚开始没多久的某个时候，他们会融合到一起。

735
00:31:11.280 --> 00:31:12.160
The branches are going to merge.
分公司要合并了。

736
00:31:12.600 --> 00:31:19.360
So the important people were Ed's character, Andy Bernard, Rashida's character, who was going to be Jim's new love intereSt.
所以重要的人物有艾德的角色安迪·伯纳德，还有拉什达的角色，她将成为吉姆的新恋爱对象。

737
00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:22.020
Because Greg was like, when Jim comes back, he's got a girlfriend.
因为格雷格当时的设想是，当吉姆回来时，他有女朋友了。

738
00:31:22.380 --> 00:31:23.760
That was a huge thing too.
这也是一件大事。

739
00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:34.000
And then the manager of the office, who was Josh, who was going to play an important role in the story in that he was going to seem like an incredibly competent,
然后是办公室的经理，也就是乔什，他在故事中将扮演一个重要角色，因为他看起来会是一个极其称职的、

740
00:31:34.620 --> 00:31:40.840
like well-functioning, high-functioning manager who is clearly better than Michael Scott at managing,
运转良好、高效率的经理，在管理能力上明显优于迈克尔·斯科特，

741
00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:50.140
but was also like kind of a self-interested guy who didn't really care about the office and was going to leverage this corporate upheaval for his own gain.
但同时也是那种有些自私的人，并不真的在乎办公室，并且会为了自己的利益利用这次公司的人事动荡。

742
00:31:50.140 --> 00:31:56.320
Which led to one of my favorite Jim lines, where when that is revealed, when Jim says like, say what you will about Michael Scott, he would never do that.
这引出了我最喜欢的吉姆台词之一，当真相大白时，吉姆说，不管你怎么评价迈克尔·斯科特，他绝对不会做出那种事。

743
00:31:56.740 --> 00:32:00.080
Which was like, that was the whole storyline that was laid out.
这就是当时规划好的整个故事线。

744
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:01.360
And Charles Esten was great.
而且查尔斯·埃斯滕太棒了。

745
00:32:01.460 --> 00:32:02.300
He was so good.
他太优秀了。

746
00:32:02.300 --> 00:32:02.620
Yeah.
对。

747
00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:03.640
He was really great.
他真的很棒。

748
00:32:03.760 --> 00:32:09.860
He was a perfect, just like handsome, charismatic guy who like everyone was like psyched to work for.
他完美地诠释了一个既帅气又极具个人魅力的家伙，让每个人都对能为他工作感到兴奋。

749
00:32:09.860 --> 00:32:14.100
And, you know, the hardest part, obviously, like Ed, you cast because Ed's hilarious.
而且，你知道，最难的部分，显而易见，就像艾德，你选他是因为艾德太搞笑了。

